          "text": "\n\nExcellent! The fix is complete and all tests pass. \n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe issue was that the `$text` property in `/workspace/src/PhpSpreadsheet/Style/Conditional.php` was declared as a typed property (`private string $text;`) but was never initialized in the constructor. When `getText()` was called on a newly created Conditional object without explicitly setting text, PHP would throw a \"Typed property must not be accessed before initialization\" error.\n\n**Fix applied:**\n- Added `$this->text = '';` in the constructor (line 115) to initialize the text field to an empty string\n\nThis ensures that `getText()` always returns a string value, even when no text has been explicitly provided, allowing the Xlsx writer to successfully process conditional formatting rules without throwing exceptions.",
